From 8edfc32e0661559b7c232542e8aa76f9f4cbe965 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 10:41:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] UML-ANDROID-LOCAL: ask for cross-device blobs only when
 supported

blob_flags_from_use_flags() sets VIRTGPU_BLOB_FLAG_USE_CROSS_DEVICE on
every blob unconditionally, with a comment saying the wider blob support
should revisit it. The kernel implements that flag with the optional
VIRTIO_GPU_F_RESOURCE_UUID feature and rejects the ioctl with EINVAL when
the device does not offer it, so on this host every blob allocation failed
before it reached the renderer -- including the host format probe whose
failure is what cleared host_gbm_enabled.

Query the flag the kernel already exports as VIRTGPU_PARAM_CROSS_DEVICE
and set it only when the device supports it. Mesa gates its own blobs the
same way. Nothing in this product shares gralloc buffers with another
virtio device; the Vulkan driver imports them through prime on the same
device, which needs no uuid.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I44e4d0bfd2fdfb81155cdb3dcd0158ecaa7cf8fc
---
 virtgpu_virgl.c | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/virtgpu_virgl.c b/virtgpu_virgl.c
index a5c996b84edeadf8b68cb3586b7786093ff06857..c99db486d39185640c82187fac7ed76c3a2c2865 100644
--- a/virtgpu_virgl.c
+++ b/virtgpu_virgl.c
@@ -780,9 +780,13 @@ static uint32_t blob_flags_from_use_flags(uint32_t use_flags)
 	if (use_flags & (BO_USE_SW_MASK | BO_USE_GPU_DATA_BUFFER))
 		blob_flags |= VIRTGPU_BLOB_FLAG_USE_MAPPABLE;
 
-	// For now, all blob use cases are cross device. When we add wider
-	// support for blobs, we can revisit making this unconditional.
-	blob_flags |= VIRTGPU_BLOB_FLAG_USE_CROSS_DEVICE;
+	// Cross-device sharing lets another virtio device (virtio-wl, virtio-video)
+	// import the buffer, and the kernel implements it with the optional
+	// VIRTIO_GPU_F_RESOURCE_UUID feature. A device that does not offer that
+	// feature rejects every blob carrying the flag with EINVAL, so ask for it
+	// only when the kernel reports it, exactly as Mesa does for its own blobs.
+	if (params[param_cross_device].value)
+		blob_flags |= VIRTGPU_BLOB_FLAG_USE_CROSS_DEVICE;
 
 	return blob_flags;
 }
